<title>UK: Rolls-Royce group gets Asian engine orders.</title>
<headline>Rolls-Royce group gets Asian engine orders.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Rolls-Royce Plc said on Tuesday it would get about $150 million from Asian orders for V2500 engines won by the company's partly-owned International Aero Engines consortium.</p>
<p>The orders, from two customers in China and Singapore, were worth up to $430 million.</p>
<p>The consortium, based in Hartford, Conn., includes United Technologies Corp's Pratt &amp; Whitney, Daimler-Benz AG's MTU, and Japanese Aero Engines Corp.</p>
